From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: pass the WCID to the WED PPE check on 7.4

Linux 7.4-rc3 extended the WED PPE check interface with the WCID of the
station the frame came from:

  include/linux/soc/mediatek/mtk_wed.h
  int (*ppe_check)(struct mtk_wed_device *dev, struct sk_buff *skb,
                   u32 reason, u32 hash, u16 wcid);
  #define mtk_wed_device_ppe_check(_dev, _skb, _reason, _hash, _wcid) ...

7.3 still takes four arguments, so a five argument call only builds on 7.4
and a four argument call only builds on 7.3.  Keep both.

Pass msta->wcid.idx, the per-station index the WED looks the binding up by;
the caller already returned early when msta is NULL.

Lead to:

  mt7996/mac.c:299:67: error: macro "mtk_wed_device_ppe_check" requires
  5 arguments, but only 4 given
  mt7996/mac.c:297:9: error: 'mtk_wed_device_ppe_check' undeclared (first
  use in this function)

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -294,9 +294,16 @@ mt7996_wed_check_ppe(struct mt7996_dev *
 	wdev = ieee80211_vif_to_wdev(vif);
 	skb->dev = wdev->netdev;
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7, 4, 0)
+	mtk_wed_device_ppe_check(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed, skb,
+				 FIELD_GET(MT_DMA_PPE_CPU_REASON, info),
+				 FIELD_GET(MT_DMA_PPE_ENTRY, info),
+				 msta->wcid.idx);
+#else
 	mtk_wed_device_ppe_check(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed, skb,
 				 FIELD_GET(MT_DMA_PPE_CPU_REASON, info),
 				 FIELD_GET(MT_DMA_PPE_ENTRY, info));
+#endif
 }
 
 static int
